516
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:14,920
 I wanted to find a different way and you need to as well.

517
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,720
 You don't wanna be Michael Corleone

518
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,880
 at the end of Godfather 2.

519
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,880
 You won, you got the house, you rule the mob,

520
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,440
 but you had to kill your family to get there

521
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:23,600
 and you're left alone.

522
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:24,760
 It's not success.

523
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:26,440
 And let me tell you something.

524
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,360
 How about you?

525
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:29,960
 Are all your prayers about you?

526
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:33,200
 Does all your money terminate on you?

527
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,520
 Is all your time to serve you?

528
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:38,160
 What Paul is saying here is that's a waste of life.

529
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:43,000
 And when you die at your funeral,

530
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,960
 we will say nice things about you.

531
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,480
 We will.

532
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:49,280
 You just want them to be true, okay?

533
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:51,240
 Makes it easier for us.

534
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,680
 Oh, she never knew a stranger.

535
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,000
 She'd give away her last dime.

536
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,720
 You don't want your family to go,

537
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:57,600
 who is he talking about right now?

538
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:00,240
 You want us all to say,

539
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:03,980
 I could tell you how that person loved me.

540
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,680
 So what does it look like?

541
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,160
 How do we actually love people?

542
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:09,000
 That's your second point.

543
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,200
 First one was a loveless life is a worthless life.

544
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:15,320
 Second thing is you gain by giving your life away.

545
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:17,080
 That's the next couple of verses.

546
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:20,160
 In verse four, he gives you sort of the positive,

547
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:21,600
 two positive statements about love.

548
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,880
 One is sort of a passive and one's an active.

549
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:27,280
 Verse four, he says, love is patient and love is kind.

550
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:29,720
 Patient is sort of the passive version of love.

551
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:32,120
 It's the word in Greek, makrosoumia.

552
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:35,080
 Soumia is heat and makros a lot.

553
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:37,680
 To be patient means I can endure the heat

554
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:40,380
 of your annoyance for a long time, right?

555
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:41,480
 That's what love is.

556
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:44,020
 I can put up with how difficult you can be.

557
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:45,240
 We live in a day right now

558
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,280
 where as soon as someone is inconvenient,

559
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:49,040
 we cut ties, go no contact.

560
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:49,920
 I'm leaving that church

561
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,160
 'cause they didn't do it exactly right.

562
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,520
 I'm breaking off that family group

563
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,360
 because she said something that's not useful for me.

564
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:57,740
 We are so quick to dismiss human beings,

565
00:21:57,740 --> 00:21:59,820
 but love does not do that.

566
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:00,660
 But it's interesting.

567
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:02,480
 There's a popular way to say it several years ago.

568
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:04,040
 People started coining the phrase,

569
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:05,800
 I am spiritual but not religious.

570
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,280
 Remember that?

571
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:08,360
 What do they mean by that?

572
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,940
 I wanna acknowledge that there's a spiritual world out there

573
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:13,040
 that can bring some value to my personal life.

574
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,300
 But when you started doing the research

575
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:15,560
 on what did you mean by religious,

576
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:17,240
 what they meant was I don't wanna be a part

577
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:19,360
 of an institutional organization,

578
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:23,120
 which what they meant was I don't want the hassle of people.

579
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:25,060
 So I wanna acknowledge the spirituality

580
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:26,080
 that benefits my life,

581
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,800
 but I don't want the inconvenience of y'all.

582
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:31,080
 And you know what's crazy about that is Paul says

583
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:33,960
 the fruit of the spirit is love, right?

584
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,960
 That the spirit give you gifts for the common good

585
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:37,400
 that you know the spirit is present

586
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:38,840
 is because you love other people.

587
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:39,800
 That means you're patient with them

588
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:40,840
 even when you're a hassle.

589
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:42,480
 And so if you say I want spirituality

590
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:43,660
 but not the hassle of people,

591
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:46,640
 you got some kind of spirit, but it's not the Holy Spirit

592
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,480
 'cause the fruit of the spirit is love,

593
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:49,840
 that I care about other people.

594
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:52,520
 And not just that I'm patient with them, that I'm kind.

595
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:55,040
 I actively pursue your benefit.

596
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,600
 I get involved in a community where,

597
00:22:57,600 --> 00:23:01,120
 look, socialization has gotten hard.

598
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:05,000
 Social media has made us all so very awkward.

599
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,060
 And so we're gonna have to be patient

600
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:09,440
 when people don't say things right.

601
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:12,440
 And we're gonna have to return to them kindness

602
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:14,420
 rather than humiliation, right?

603
00:23:14,420 --> 00:23:15,360
 What is true love?

604
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:18,040
 It is patient and it is kind.

605
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:20,520
 And then he tells you seven things it doesn't do.

606
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:21,960
 Which is interesting, we don't have time to go into this,

607
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:24,100
 but where does he get this list, by the way?

608
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:25,880
 Love is not envy, it does not boast.

609
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,280
 Was Paul just pontificating?

610
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,640
 What is love, Paul?

611
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:30,040
 Hmm, don't hurt me.

612
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:32,400
 You know, like, what is he doing?

613
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:35,320
 If you read 1 Corinthians 1 through 12,

614
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:37,760
 all the stuff he's gonna say to not do in this next part

615
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,520
 was the stuff they were doing.

616
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:41,380
 So Paul literally gets his definition from you like,

617
00:23:41,380 --> 00:23:42,220
 you know what you guys are doing?

618
00:23:42,220 --> 00:23:43,760
 Yeah, yeah, it's the opposite of that.

619
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:45,040
 Like you're doing it 100% wrong.

620
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:46,320
 So he's just saying like,

621
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,480
 it's the opposite of what y'all are up to.

622
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:51,880
 So he says, love does not envy and love does not boast.

623
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:55,680
 Envy is you have something I want and I feel bad about it.

624
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:57,680
 Boast is I have something you want

625
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:59,320
 and so I make you feel bad about it.

626
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:02,480
 But either way, it ends with people feeling bad.

627
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:05,060
 Love does not envy, that means it doesn't resent people

628
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:07,580
 for having what I want.

629
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:10,480
 When you start mixing in with other humans,

630
00:24:10,480 --> 00:24:12,700
 you're gonna meet people that have a better job than you,

631
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:14,600
 make more money than you, have a boat that you have,

632
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:16,560
 have more vacation time, and what's gonna happen?

633
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:18,040
 For some of you, you're gonna see that person

634
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:19,640
 who has the things you want and you're gonna go,

635
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:21,800
 you know what, I hate that guy.

636
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:23,720
 I don't like his face, he's got a punchable face.

637
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:25,500
 That's how I feel about it, right?

638
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:28,680
 But if you get underneath it, you just realize,

639
00:24:28,680 --> 00:24:31,380
 I just envy him, I wish I had what he had.

640
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:34,840
 It was interesting, when I first started to preach,

641
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,360
 you know, I had my little youth group of one,

642
00:24:36,360 --> 00:24:39,600
 it began to grow and after I got to about 50 kids or so,

643
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:42,360
 I started getting called to speak at other places.

644
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:44,580
 And I didn't know is I would drive around Texas

645
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:45,700
 and speak at these other places.

646
00:24:45,700 --> 00:24:48,380
 I didn't realize I was backfilling a guy

647
00:24:48,380 --> 00:24:51,700
 that had moved to Dallas and yet I would start speaking

648
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:53,300
 at these places and I'm just studying the Bible,

649
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:55,080
 trying to help kids know God and at the end of it,

650
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:56,800
 I would stand down front to pray with anybody

651
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:58,440
 who wanted to be prayed for and minister to people

652
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:00,360
 and I would get this line of people that wanted to come

653
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:02,280
 and I'm like, oh, man, God's really convicted their soul

654
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:03,360
 through my preaching, that's great.

655
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:05,680
 And so these kids would come down and one after another,

656
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:08,380
 someone would come up to me and go, hey man, great job.

657
00:25:08,380 --> 00:25:10,640
 You ever heard Matt Chandler?

658
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:13,060
 Man, he's good.

659
00:25:13,060 --> 00:25:15,160
 I mean, you did fine, but he's the guy that just left

660
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:18,400
 and wow, wow, he's amazing, you should check him out.

661
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:19,680
 I'm like, okay, thanks.

662
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:20,760
 And like the first kid, I was like,

663
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:21,800
 well, that's kind of weird.

664
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:24,760
 After a kid like 40, 50, 60, I was like, okay,

665
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:27,440
 you know what, I'm doing my best up here.

666
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:32,440
 And I started to resent this guy I'd never met.

667
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:35,080
 And I realized I had seen the movie Mozart.

668
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:35,920
 I don't know if you ever saw that.

669
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:37,900
 Well, Salieri hates Mozart talent and goes nuts

670
00:25:37,900 --> 00:25:38,740
 and ends up killing him.

671
00:25:38,740 --> 00:25:39,600
 I was like, I don't wanna be that guy.

672
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:41,040
 That's a bad story and that's the wrong guy

673
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,400
 to be in the story.

674
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:45,400
 But I feel envy, how do you stop it?

675
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:48,280
 And I realized the only way to stop it was to pray

676
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:50,680
 and not to pray for me 'cause that didn't work.

677
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,960
 I started praying for him.

678
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,680
 And I started to pray for Matt Chandler.

679
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:57,740
 I started to pray for his times in the Bible,

680
00:25:57,740 --> 00:25:59,000
 his quiet times.

681
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,320
 Started to pray for his marriage.

682
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:02,280
 Started to pray for his kids.

683
00:26:02,280 --> 00:26:04,920
 There were moments in my young 20s and 30s

684
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:09,680
 where I would cry praying for God to bless this man

685
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:11,240
 and I didn't know him.

686
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:14,520
 And so when I moved to Dallas and we became friends,

687
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:16,320
 I already loved him.

688
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:18,880
 And it's because love doesn't envy.

689
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:21,600
 I wanna see you win and it sets me free.

690
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:24,120
 It doesn't boast.

691
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:26,760
 Boasting is I got something that you don't have

692
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:29,080
 so I like to talk about it to make me feel important.

693
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:31,640
 But you notice, does anyone really love that?

694
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:32,840
 Hey, I saw you talking to Bob, how'd it go?

695
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:33,660
 Oh, it was great.

696
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:34,600
 He was telling me about all the stuff he has

697
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:36,080
 that I didn't have and how great he is.

698
00:26:36,080 --> 00:26:37,520
 I just felt so encouraged.

699
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:39,080
 I love that, that was neat.

700
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:42,000
 No one wants to hear it, man.

701
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:44,120
 Love doesn't envy and love doesn't boast.

702
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:45,720
 It's not arrogant, that is proud.

703
00:26:45,720 --> 00:26:47,640
 It's not rude, which is mean to other people.

704
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:49,080
 It doesn't insist on its own way.

705
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:50,400
 Everything's gotta be just how I like it

706
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,800
 or else I'm gonna complain.

707
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:53,880
 It's not irritable, that means easily upset

708
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:54,780
 or it's not resentful.

709
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:57,760
 That means I hold on to grudges for a long time.

710
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:59,400
 It's interesting, I'm reading the memoirs

711
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:02,760
 of Ulysses S. Grant right now and I'm right in the center.

712
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:04,400
 He's fighting the Civil War, it's going pretty good.

713
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:06,960
 I don't know how it's gonna end, it's very exciting.

714
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:11,960
 But the greatest problem Ulysses S. Grant is running into

715
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:17,000
 is not the other army with their weapons.

716
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:20,760
 Right now his greatest problem is there's people

717
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:22,080
 that don't wanna follow his orders

718
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:24,320
 because they weren't given just so.

719
00:27:24,320 --> 00:27:26,100
 Or there's people that don't wanna serve in that role

720
00:27:26,100 --> 00:27:27,600
 because that means they'd be under that person

721
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:28,840
 and that person's younger and I shouldn't be

722
00:27:28,840 --> 00:27:30,200
 under that person and that shouldn't be that way.

723
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:35,200
 And it's the problem that almost unraveled America

724
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:38,620
 was the ego of a handful of people.

725
00:27:38,620 --> 00:27:42,080
 And you see to be a selfish, egotistical person,

726
00:27:42,080 --> 00:27:42,920
 it's terrible.

727
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:45,520
 We launched a church in Washington, D.C.

728
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:47,960
 Our church, 2/3 of them are under 30, 2/3 are singles,

729
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:50,440
 very young deal, and when we launched the church,

730
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:51,460
 we were meeting in a bar.

731
00:27:51,460 --> 00:27:52,840
 So when we showed up Sunday morning,

732
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,320
 it's like you never knew what was gonna happen

733
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:55,160
 when you showed up.

734
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,480
 Our first Sunday, the night before

735
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:58,640
 had been the St. Patrick's Day smokeout.

736
00:27:58,640 --> 00:28:01,080
 The hit song of the band that played was the Doobie Ashtray

737
00:28:01,080 --> 00:28:03,080
 and that's what the room was like.

738
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:04,080
 And so it was amazing.

739
00:28:04,080 --> 00:28:06,000
 We would routinely wake people up on stage

740
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,160
 that had been there through the night before

741
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,680
 and we're like, hey man, you don't have to leave,

742
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:09,600
 but you gotta scooch.

743
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:11,600
 Like we gotta put the speakers up here.

744
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:12,800
 And so it was kind of a wild ride.

745
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:14,200
 You never knew what you were gonna run into.

746
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,200
 And we had people that worked for every agency,

747
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:18,960
 every branch of the government, all through politics,

748
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:21,560
 mopping up puke and picking up dead rats

749
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:22,800
 and all kinds of stuff,

750
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:24,880
 just doing this incredible service

751
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:27,000
 to help other people know God.

752
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,480
 And I remember one Sunday afterwards,

753
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:29,920
 people were stacking chairs

754
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:31,360
 and this guy came up to me and he was like,

755
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:34,200
 hey man, this is great what's happening here.

756
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,960
 You need some help around here?

757
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:36,800
 And I was like, yeah, man,

758
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:38,460
 right now we need help stacking these chairs.

759
00:28:38,460 --> 00:28:41,200
 Like if you wanna jump in, he was like, no, no, no.

760
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:43,360
 Like I sort of have a prophetic ministry.

761
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:44,800
 I get on stage and I speak to people

762
00:28:44,800 --> 00:28:45,880
 and they fall out with the Holy Spirit.

763
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:46,720
 It's very powerful.

764
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,720
 People repent and change people's lives.

765
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:49,280
 So like, if you need some help with that, let me know.

766
00:28:49,280 --> 00:28:51,320
 I was like, yeah, man, I'll let you know.

767
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,160
 Yeah, great.

768
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:53,680
 But if you wanna help out, we gotta stack those chairs

769
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:55,240
 because there's a band coming in at about three

770
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:56,080
 and we gotta get out of here.

771
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:57,880
 And he was like, yeah, no, you don't understand.

772
00:28:57,880 --> 00:29:01,640
 Like I get on stage and I speak to people.

773
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:02,880
 I was like, yeah, you don't understand,

774
