 And I knew that his parents had just divorced

1035
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:21,400
 and I knew he had spent that weekend

1036
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:23,860
 helping his dad move into his apartment downtown.

1037
00:38:23,860 --> 00:38:26,100
 And he said, I'm fine.

1038
00:38:26,100 --> 00:38:28,880
 And I said, hey man, and I don't normally

1039
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:30,080
 talk about like this to kids.

1040
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:32,000
 I was like, hey man, I know God's gonna take care of you.

1041
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,120
 I know you'll be fine.

1042
00:38:33,120 --> 00:38:35,200
 But this sucks.

1043
00:38:35,200 --> 00:38:37,740
 And it's okay to say it sucks.

1044
00:38:37,740 --> 00:38:41,720
 And as soon as I said that, he just started crying.

1045
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:44,240
 And he just fell into my arms.

1046
00:38:44,240 --> 00:38:46,100
 Little 11, 12 year old kid.

1047
00:38:46,100 --> 00:38:50,120
 And I realized, where else can he go?

1048
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:52,720
 It's fine is what he keeps hearing from his parents.

1049
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:55,080
 His buddies don't know how to care for him.

1050
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:57,640
 But I know 'cause I've been there.

1051
00:38:57,640 --> 00:38:59,840
 And rather than just moving on to build my empire,

1052
00:38:59,840 --> 00:39:01,220
 I turned back and see this kid

1053
00:39:01,220 --> 00:39:02,200
 and I remember as I held him,

1054
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:05,700
 I thought about all that it cost me

1055
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:08,480
 to be a single guy just serving in my church.

1056
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:09,920
 And I thought, you know what?

1057
00:39:09,920 --> 00:39:11,520
 It's worth it.

1058
00:39:11,520 --> 00:39:12,960
 It's worth it.

1059
00:39:12,960 --> 00:39:14,680
 'Cause when I race on into forever,

1060
00:39:14,680 --> 00:39:16,800
 into the sunrise of the face of Jesus,

1061
00:39:16,800 --> 00:39:19,160
 I gotta wake a kid's behind me that know him

1062
00:39:19,160 --> 00:39:20,120
 'cause I existed.

1063
00:39:20,120 --> 00:39:23,000
 And friend, that's not just for me, that's for you.

1064
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:25,360
 So I wanna encourage you, start now, don't wait.

1065
00:39:25,360 --> 00:39:27,960
 Let's be great at loving us.

1066
00:39:27,960 --> 00:39:30,080
 This is the moment, this is the time, this is us.

1067
00:39:30,080 --> 00:39:32,240
 It's not some hypothetical propositional people later.

1068
00:39:32,240 --> 00:39:33,200
 This is us.

1069
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:38,500
 In DC, we had snowmageddon this last December.

1070
00:39:38,500 --> 00:39:39,760
 I know you're not as familiar.

1071
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:41,620
 It's when rain gets really cold.

1072
00:39:41,620 --> 00:39:43,920
 And then it can stick to the ground,

1073
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:44,880
 it makes it really hard to drive.

1074
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:47,560
 And so it just sucked in the city for like a week.

1075
00:39:47,560 --> 00:39:49,040
 No one could move.

1076
00:39:49,040 --> 00:39:52,040
 And so all this snow and ice was blocking people in.

1077
00:39:52,040 --> 00:39:52,880
 And it was interesting.

1078
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:54,600
 I was standing at where our church meets in this theater.

1079
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:56,720
 And you know, you look up and DC is a high density city.

1080
00:39:56,720 --> 00:39:58,320
 All these people living in these big apartments.

1081
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:01,440
 And man, as the city just wore on day after day after day

1082
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:02,540
 of lockdown, no one could drive.

1083
00:40:02,540 --> 00:40:04,440
 What do you think we all did together?

1084
00:40:04,440 --> 00:40:07,880
 We all got on our phones and complained about it.

1085
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:10,040
 Look at the snow, somebody better do something.

1086
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:11,960
 Somebody, somebody, something, something.

1087
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:14,080
 And you know what that accomplished?

1088
00:40:14,080 --> 00:40:16,200
 Nothing positive.

1089
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,720
 And finally I sat there, I was looking around.

1090
00:40:17,720 --> 00:40:20,800
 I was like, does no one own a shovel?

1091
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:24,040
 Can you lease one with an option to buy?

1092
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:26,440
 I was like, there's so many humans on this block

1093
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:30,800
 that we can clear these blocks in 15 minutes.

1094
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:31,640
 I thought, you know what?

1095
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:32,800
 I can't control them.

1096
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:34,700
 Let me just call some of my people and say, hey, let's go.

1097
00:40:34,700 --> 00:40:37,000
 Let's just get shovels and handle it.

1098
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:38,400
 And so we got out there and started shoveling.

1099
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:39,680
 I'll tell you the craziest thing happened

1100
00:40:39,680 --> 00:40:41,240
 as we started to do that.

1101
00:40:41,240 --> 00:40:42,480
 People are walking down the streets,

1102
00:40:42,480 --> 00:40:43,320
 tripping over snow,

1103
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:45,360
 trying to climb snow banks to get to their doors.

1104
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:47,120
 And they would look at us and they would say,

1105
00:40:47,120 --> 00:40:48,520
 you with the city?

1106
00:40:48,520 --> 00:40:51,000
 Like, no, dog, do I look like I'm with the city?

1107
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:52,360
 Like, no, I'm not with the city.

1108
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:53,720
 (audience laughing)

1109
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:54,680
 And then it was the most interesting thing,

1110
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:56,240
 'cause in D.C. everyone's important,

1111
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:58,320
 more important than you in trying to get somewhere fast.

1112
00:40:58,320 --> 00:41:00,960
 So you just walk by and throw a shoulder and go, go, go.

1113
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:01,800
 They would stop.

1114
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:02,760
 They were so confused.

1115
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:03,600
 You with the city?

1116
00:41:03,600 --> 00:41:04,560
 No.

1117
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:06,000
 You're just a guy doing this?

1118
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:09,080
 That's amazing.

1119
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:11,280
 Changed my view of humanity.

1120
00:41:11,280 --> 00:41:13,680
 You know, they just didn't know how to handle it.

1121
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:16,540
 And there was this warmth on our block

1122
00:41:16,540 --> 00:41:19,440
 that didn't exist minutes before.

1123
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,680
 And I'm just telling you, family,

1124
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:22,940
 I know we got a lot of hopes in here,

1125
00:41:22,940 --> 00:41:25,000
 but if all your hopes are just to build your money,

1126
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:27,200
 your fame, your power, your success,

1127
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:28,920
 Paul's saying it's a waste of life.

1128
00:41:28,920 --> 00:41:31,760
 A much better life is love.

1129
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:33,000
 Love us.

1130
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:33,840
 Just go, you know what?

1131
00:41:33,840 --> 00:41:34,680
 I do have some hopes.

1132
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:35,880
 God, I want business success.

1133
00:41:35,880 --> 00:41:36,720
 I wanna get married.

1134
00:41:36,720 --> 00:41:37,540
 I want these things.

1135
00:41:37,540 --> 00:41:38,380
 I can't control all that.

1136
00:41:38,380 --> 00:41:39,320
 I put that at your feet,

1137
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:41,500
 but what I can do is pick up a shovel.

1138
00:41:41,500 --> 00:41:43,280
 I can step up and serve.

1139
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:44,640
 I can try to figure out how I'm gifted

1140
00:41:44,640 --> 00:41:46,000
 and just jump in and play the game.

1141
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:48,120
 I can go to a church and get involved.

1142
00:41:48,120 --> 00:41:51,460
 I can help some kids behind me get a better leg up on life.

1143
00:41:51,460 --> 00:41:53,800
 My dad came to faith

1144
00:41:53,800 --> 00:41:58,020
 'cause some man volunteered at the hospital.

1145
00:41:58,020 --> 00:42:01,400
 And he'd walk by rooms and knock on the door,

1146
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:03,480
 say, "Hey, I'm just here volunteering.

1147
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:04,580
 "Can I pray with you?"

1148
00:42:04,580 --> 00:42:07,240
 And then it was funny when he came to my dad's room,

1149
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:08,400
 he said, "Hey, can I pray with you?

1150
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:10,320
 "Or do you wanna confess anything?"

1151
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:13,120
 My dad thought that was the craziest thing to say.

1152
00:42:13,120 --> 00:42:15,740
 My dad said, "Bro, if I confess everything,

1153
00:42:15,740 --> 00:42:18,160
 "you're gonna be here a long time."

1154
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,960
 And he said, "That's okay, I'm retired."

1155
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:20,880
 And he sat down.

1156
00:42:20,880 --> 00:42:23,160
 (congregation laughing)

1157
00:42:23,160 --> 00:42:26,080
 And some random guy I don't know held my dad's hand

1158
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:28,480
 and prayed with him and changed his life.

1159
00:42:28,480 --> 00:42:29,320
 Changed his life.

1160
00:42:29,320 --> 00:42:32,880
 I came to faith in Jesus

1161
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:34,480
 'cause some woman whose name I don't remember

1162
00:42:34,480 --> 00:42:36,800
 volunteered in the nursery.

1163
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:38,480
 And one day, and I don't know what she saw

1164
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:39,640
 or did not see in me,

1165
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:41,440
 but she was like, "Hey, Ben, sidebar."

1166
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:44,000
 And sat down and just told me about the love of Jesus

1167
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,640
 that could save even me.

1168
00:42:45,640 --> 00:42:46,480
 And I believed.

1169
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:49,480
 I know you got hopes, I know you got dreams,

1170
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:51,080
 but you know what you got also?

1171
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:53,880
 You got a chance to change the world right now.

1172
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:55,580
 And yes, it'll be through your gifts,

1173
00:42:55,580 --> 00:42:57,960
 but your gifts used in service of love.

1174
00:42:57,960 --> 00:43:00,640
 'Cause a loveless life's a wasted one.

1175
00:43:00,640 --> 00:43:02,640
 But you will gain by giving away

1176
00:43:02,640 --> 00:43:05,480
 because the love you show now raises honor to forever.

1177
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:08,120
 So, Father, thank you.

1178
00:43:08,120 --> 00:43:12,640
 Thank you that Jesus was patient.

1179
00:43:14,080 --> 00:43:15,680
 And thank you that he was kind.

1180
00:43:15,680 --> 00:43:19,760
 Thank you, God, that he bore all things,

1181
00:43:19,760 --> 00:43:22,280
 our sin on the cross,

1182
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:25,820
 because of the hope set before him,

1183
00:43:25,820 --> 00:43:28,080
 that he knew he could save sinners like us.

1184
00:43:28,080 --> 00:43:31,040
 God, none of us love as we ought,

1185
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:34,780
 but thank you that we have been loved so much by Jesus

1186
00:43:34,780 --> 00:43:37,200
 that it can change us from the inside out.

1187
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:38,880
 And friends, some of you, you didn't get the love

1188
00:43:38,880 --> 00:43:40,920
 you should have by your parents.

1189
00:43:40,920 --> 00:43:43,720
 You've lived in a cold world and sin has broken everything.

1190
00:43:43,720 --> 00:43:45,920
 But let me tell you something, God loves you.

1191
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:48,420
 You're broken 'cause of sin,

1192
00:43:48,420 --> 00:43:54,520
 but Jesus came because God so loved the world

1193
00:43:54,520 --> 00:43:56,320
 that he gave his son,

1194
00:43:56,320 --> 00:43:58,380
 that whoever believes would not perish,

1195
00:43:58,380 --> 00:43:59,840
 but have everlasting life.

1196
00:43:59,840 --> 00:44:02,720
 Greater love has no man than this,

1197
00:44:02,720 --> 00:44:04,940
 and he laid down his life for his friends.

1198
00:44:04,940 --> 00:44:07,780
 And Jesus laid down his life for you, friend.

1199
00:44:07,780 --> 00:44:10,380
 You put your faith in him today and let him change you.

1200
00:44:11,600 --> 00:44:14,500
 And God, I pray the men in here would be oaks in the city.

1201
00:44:14,500 --> 00:44:17,640
 I pray the women would be shade

1202
00:44:17,640 --> 00:44:19,300
 for the hurting and the hopeless.

1203
00:44:19,300 --> 00:44:21,800
 And God, I pray right here in this room,

1204
00:44:21,800 --> 00:44:26,800
 we would be a grove of trees standing strong in Dallas

1205
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:28,840
 that as Jesus said in the last days,

1206
00:44:28,840 --> 00:44:31,040
 the love of many grows cold.

1207
00:44:31,040 --> 00:44:34,160
 But I would say, we would say right here at the porch,

1208
00:44:34,160 --> 00:44:36,960
 not us, not us.

1209
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:38,880
 Our love is white hot,

1210
00:44:38,880 --> 00:44:42,280
 burning because we've been loved and we love.

1211
00:44:42,280 --> 00:44:45,440
 And God, I pray you'd bless us for your glory and our good.

1212
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:46,280
 In Jesus' name.

